# Educational Use Only Licence — Version 1.0

**Project:** `analysy` — Educational Malware Analysis Lab
**Covered material:** the documentation, analysis notes, YARA rules and
scripts authored for this repository (the "Material").
**Date of publication:** 2026-11-07

---

## 0. Plain-language summary (non-binding)

This repository may be **read, studied, quoted and taught from** by anyone who
wants to learn how malware and game cheats are built and detected. It may
**not** be used to run the sample, to cheat in a game, to bypass anti-cheat or
security software, to build or distribute malware, or to make money. The
sample itself is somebody else's software: it is here as evidence, and this
licence gives you no rights over it.

If the summary and the numbered terms ever disagree, the numbered terms win.

---

## 1. Definitions

1.1 **"Material"** means the original text, tables, analysis notes, YARA rules,
configuration and source code created by the author and distributed in this
repository, including `README.md`, `analysis/*`, `yara/*` and `tools/*`.

1.2 **"Sample"** means the third-party binary distributed alongside the
Material, currently the file `linou free.exe` (SHA-256
`7d2c55b9d95203e966f70e5de8a04aa48daccd7a1b5ff9d0b17f5a9a06bc085a`), together
with every embedded component it contains (loader, cheat DLL, kernel driver,
downloaded content). The Sample is **not** part of the Material and is **not**
licensed to you under this document.

1.3 **"Author"** means the contributor(s) of the Material to this repository.

1.4 **"Educational Purpose"** means private study, teaching, academic research,
CTF/training exercises, detection engineering (writing signatures, rules,
heuristics, sandbox/EDR logic), and defensive security work — in each case on
systems and artefacts you own or are expressly authorised in writing to analyse.

1.5 **"Prohibited Purpose"** means any use not covered by Section 2, including
without limitation those listed in Section 3.

